<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Massacre of Najran</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">523</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Martyrs of Najran</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Massacre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najran">Najran</a> was the killing of the Christian community of Najran, in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, in 523 by the Himyarite king Yusuf As'ar Yath'ar, known in Arab tradition as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhu-nuwas">Dhu Nuwas</a>, who had adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>. Reports of the martyrs reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksum</a>, and in 525 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaleb">King Kaleb</a> of Aksum crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a>, overthrew Yusuf and installed a Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>.</p></div>
